# Build output. Every asset tree is generated from `src/**` + `docs/**`:
#   `pnpm build`  -> `public/` (the deployable tree; one release per channel is written into it)
#   `pnpm dev`    -> `public-dev/` (the tree `wrangler dev` serves)
# `public/` is tracked: the committed tree is what gets deployed, which is what makes a
# published release reviewable and `scripts/verify-committed.ts` means something. `public-dev/` is
# not: `vite build --watch` rewrites it while a dev session runs.
public-dev/

# docs
docs/tmp
